      "note": "witnesses_fast with m = 3 and a sink that never stops, so the whole base is walked. It sits 77.6 ns a base point above the blocked row on BOTH tables (to within a tenth) - that is add_many's batched inversion plus the recovery an admitted key pays, and it is a different quantity from the 74 ns that separates this row's two columns. The steadiest row, because it averages over the whole base rather than 200000 sampled probes."
