  "the_conclusion": "The fold's cost in the descent is 74 ns a base point, and the canonicalisation measured alone is 76. There is no unexplained remainder: the ~144 ns a lone probe pays over the canon is the memory round trip the block overlaps and the fused loop does not.",
  "why_blocking_pays": {
    "what_is_established": "The key is ~76 ns of dependent work before the address it will load is known, and that length is what stops consecutive probes' round trips overlapping when fused. The control is the compact table, whose key is a pack: it gains 1.35x where the folded table gains 1.83x.",
    "chunk_1_control": "1.00x on the folded table, so the figure is the blocking and not the buffer the chunked loop uses.",
    "not_lane_interleaving": "A separate thing, measured elsewhere and worth nothing here: interleaving fills one dependency chain's latency with another chain's work, and a rotation has no chain to fill. Blocking lets the memory accesses overlap.",
    "prefetch": "The descent also prefetches 32 keys ahead. Measured on top of the blocking it is worth a few per cent, not the effect."
  },
