  "still_one_at_a_time": "The m = 4 arm of witnesses_fast_inner walks every second half R - (P_k + P_l) and calls pairs_for on each, so it pays the 265 rather than the 145. Quadratic in the base and the least used; not changed here.",
  "not_claimed": [
    "Which microarchitectural resource the long key exhausts. Reorder-buffer capacity fits; so would the data-dependent branch in the rotation's x < best; and a 128 MiB filter walked at random misses the TLB on most probes. Nothing measured here separates them. The compact control speaks to the key's LENGTH being the cause, not to the mechanism by which length costs.",
    "That the mechanism is L1 eviction between the canon's 16 KiB tables and the table's random lines. Three random lines a probe out of a 768-line L1 does not account for the gap, and the shape of the chunk sweep - most of the gain already at c = 16 - does not fit a re-warming story.",
    "That these absolute numbers combine with any other run's. Same host across these three, different from the bucket-hash run."
  ]
